FUN_1000_852f base-loss on the INDIA3 op-0x2c paint.

Asm 0x1852f: `lea bx,[bx+4]; mov ax,[bx]; inc ax; mov bx,[bx+2]; add bx,3; call 52d1` --
param_1 (bx) is a DGROUP NEAR OFFSET, and [bx+4]/[bx+6] are DS-relative reads (SS=DS=DGROUP).
Likewise `mov di,ds:0x6d34; test [di+0x40],1` reads word[DS:[2d34]+0x40].  Ghidra typed param_1
and DAT_2000_2d34 as host pointers and deref'd them raw -> SIGSEGV (param_1=0x7ff4).  Rebase the
three DS-relative reads onto g_mem+0x1c000 (16-bit wrap); widths match the asm (WORD).  52d1 gets
coords (word+1 / word+3), unchanged.
